// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Launch Agent/Daemon Masquerading As Apple
// Sigma ID: 5d1b6981-6999-4da8-9f82-22410cad9c37
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Bouliw
// Date: 2026-10-12 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, stealth, T1543.001, T1543.004, T1036.005
// Description: Detects the creation of a launch agent or launch daemon property list named after Apple
//   ("com.apple.*") outside of "/System/Library". macOS ships its own launch agents and daemons in
//   "/System/Library", so a "com.apple.*" plist written to "/Library/LaunchAgents",
//   "/Library/LaunchDaemons" or a user's "~/Library/LaunchAgents" is likely a program hiding behind
//   Apple's name to persist. EvilQuest installed "com.apple.questd.plist" in both
//   "/Library/LaunchDaemons" and "~/Library/LaunchAgents", and CookieMiner installed
//   "com.apple.rig2.plist" in "~/Library/LaunchAgents".
// False positives:
//   - Apple software installed outside of macOS that ships its own launch agents or daemons
// References:
//   - https://www.intego.com/mac-security-blog/new-mac-ransomware-spyware-thiefquest-in-the-wild/
//   - https://objective-see.org/blog/blog_0x53.html
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/mac-malware-steals-cryptocurrency-exchanges-cookies/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/d9ef722b35e2d5230e3b1d7fe4b5c106ef086dfd/rules/macos/file_event/file_event_macos_launch_item_masquerading_as_apple.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where ((FolderPath contains "/Library/LaunchAgents/com.apple." or FolderPath contains "/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.apple.") and FolderPath endswith ".plist") and (not((FolderPath in~ ("/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.apple.installer.cleanupinstaller.plist") or FolderPath startswith "/System/Library/")))
